Codes and data to implement IPM on Centaurea corymbosa


List of contributors (in alphabetic order)

Adèle Erlichman
Hélène Fréville
Asma Hadjou Bel Aid
Eric Imbert
Sandrine Maurice
Loic Pages
Ophélie Ronce
François Rousset



Data are stored in the data directory

Step 1 : ModelSelection.Rmd
	Model selections and creation of a R object named SelectedModels.RData with several selected models for each vital rate


Step 2 
For each vital rate, there is a specific script to run selected models in Step 1 and make comparisons


Step 3 : ModelSelectionReport.Rmd
Once a specific model has been choosen for each vital rate, each selected model is renamed and
a R object named VitalRates.RData is created and ready to be imported in the IPM script


Step 4 : IPM.Rmd for a global IPM, but more interesting is IPM_Pop_Year.Rmd to compute kernals for each combination Population*Year.
Also included IPM per population (pooling data over years) and IPM per year (pooling data among populations).

